# GENERATED OUTPUT GOES TO scratch/, NEVER THE REPO ROOT.
#
# Run transcripts, aborted bench runs, redirected logs, applied patches. One
# run's output, not part of the build. A result worth keeping is written into a
# notes file; superseded evidence goes to docs/evidence/<date>-<name>-INVALID.txt
# with a header saying what produced it and why it is wrong.
scratch/

# The old transcript names stay ignored wherever they land, because they used to
# be written next to the repo and a stale one reported a wrong result for days.
depthcheck*.txt
depthsurvey*.txt
survey*.txt

# File deliveries from a Claude session land here. One conversation's
# attachments, not part of the build, and `dev dead` scans source trees.
Claude outputs/
.venv/
mask_overlays/

# What the pipeline chose from, written by `segment_hosted.dump_masks` when
# NUTRIAI_MASK_DUMP is set (`dev api` sets it). One scan's binary masks -- an
# input to a replay, not part of the build, and it grows with every scan.
mask_dumps/

# `dev api` tees into here, one file per server start, so evidence capture is
# never something anyone has to remember. Untracked by default -- a server that
# runs all day would otherwise dirty the tree on every restart. When a run
# matters, commit a copy under its own name (see the photo-35 files here).
docs/evidence/api-*.txt

backend/.env*
*keys*.txt
